Third-party components and attribution
------------------------------------------------------------------------

This repository is an independent PyTorch reimplementation ("port") of the
embedding model from Google Research's Perch 2.0. It is not produced or
endorsed by Google.

Perch 2.0
  - Model, architecture, and trained weights: Google Research.
  - Released under the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  - Source: https://github.com/google-research/perch
    and the Kaggle "google/bird-vocalization-classifier" (Perch 2.0) model.
  - This repository DOES NOT redistribute Perch 2.0 weights. The weights are
    regenerated locally by the user via extract_weights.py from    
    Google's published model (see README, "Getting the weights").

ONNX export
  - justinchuby/Perch-onnx: an ONNX conversion of Google's TF Perch 2.0 model.
  - https://huggingface.co/justinchuby/Perch-onnx
  - Used here as a validation oracle and as the source the weight-extraction
    script reads. Not claimed as this project's work.

Labels / taxonomy
  - cgeorgiaw/Perch (iNaturalist taxonomy), as published with the model.

EfficientNet
  - EfficientNet architecture: Tan & Le, "EfficientNet: Rethinking Model
    Scaling for Convolutional Neural Networks," 2019.

perch-hoplite
  - Google Research's agile-modeling toolkit used (core, TensorFlow-free) for
    the embedding database and search/classifier workflow.
  - https://github.com/google-research/perch-hoplite

Trademarks and model names ("Perch", "Perch 2.0", "Grace Blackwell", "NVIDIA")
are the property of their respective owners and are used here for identification
only.
